  "id": "COMPOUND:22013 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between the compound in question and HepG2 cells. The compound, (15S,1R,2R,13R)-5,15-Bis(3-methylbut-2-enyl)-6,8-dihydroxy-17,17-dimethyl-3,16-dioxapentacyclo[11.4.1.0<2,11>.0<2,15>.0<4,9>]octadeca-4(9),5,7,11-tetraene-10,14-dione, is identified as a target of multiple entities, including SNU-387 and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion. These entities are themselves targets of HepG2, indicating a potential pathway where the compound may interact with HepG2 through these intermediates. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator or activator of HepG2, possibly through a mechanism involving the activation of signaling pathways or the binding to specific receptors. The consistent presence of the compound as a target of multiple entities, all of which are targets of HepG2, supports the hypothesis that the compound may have a direct or indirect effect on HepG2 cells, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
